  "cil_liability": false,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would provide an unacceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers by reason of the inadequate provision of natural light and outlook to the ground floor communal living space. The proposed conversion of the existing conservatory to cycle storage would substantially diminish the availability of natural light and outlook, leaving the communal living area primarily reliant upon a small side-facing window. As a consequence, the communal living space would be poorly lit, provide a poor sense of enclosure and limited outlook, and fail to provide a satisfactory level of residential amenity, resulting in substandard living conditions for future occupants. The proposal would therefore be contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP4 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and paragraphs 131 and 139(f) of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), which seek to secure high-quality design and a high standard of amenity for future occupants.",
    "The proposed development has failed to demonstrate that it would be safe from flood risk for its lifetime. In the absence of a satisfactory Flood Risk Assessment and Flood Management/Evacuation Plan, insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the proposed ground-floor sleeping accommodation would be adequately protected from the risk of surface water flooding during the 1 in 100-year rainfall event, including an appropriate allowance for climate change. Furthermore, it has not been demonstrated that future occupants would have access to safe refuge and safe means of escape in the event of flooding. The proposal therefore fails to adequately manage and mitigate flood risk and would place future occupants at an unacceptable risk of harm. As such, the proposal is contrary to Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD59, DMD60, DMD61 and DMD62 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the Enfield Strategic Flood Risk Assessment (2008)."
  ]
}